@inject Odyssey.ApiClient.Resources.IProfileApiClient ProfileApi
@*
    UserProfileMark — the /users identity mark: a user's profile picture where they have one, the
    role-tinted initials monogram where they do not (issue #94 §3, Odyssey Design System · Users kit).

    PRESENCE IS THE ROW'S OWN `ExistingUser.ProfileImageVersion` TOKEN, never a probe of the byte
    endpoint. That is what lets a 50-row page render with ZERO speculative requests: a null token
    emits no <img> at all, so an administratively disabled subject — whose token the server nulls —
    produces no request, no 404 and no flicker to the monogram.

    THE FAILED STATE IS PER ROW, and this component is the row. OdsAvatar.OnError only invokes the
    callback and holds no flag, so the consumer owns it; one page-level flag would blank every avatar
    after a single failure. It is keyed on the token, so a replace retries.

    THE TINT TRAVELS AS Bg/Fg, NEVER AS A CLASS. The role tints are declared in Users.razor.css, which
    is SCOPED — scoped CSS does not cross a component boundary, so a `Class` would silently do nothing
    and every monogram would fall back to the default.

    ALT TEXT FOLLOWS WHAT THE IMAGE IS, and the two call sites differ: in a LIST ROW the adjacent cell
    names the person, so the mark is decorative (Alt=""); in the DETAIL PANEL the neighbour is a mono
    user id rather than a name, so it carries the subject's resolved display name. That is the caller's
    call, passed in — never guessed here.

    A load failure is silent. No broken-image glyph, no toast: an identity token that cannot load is
    not the user's problem to act on.
*@

@if (ShowImage)
{
    <OdsAvatar Size="Size" Src="@ImageSrc" Alt="@Alt" OnError="OnImageError" />
}
else
{
    <OdsAvatar Size="Size" Initials="@UserDisplay.Initials(User)" Alt="@Alt"
               Bg="@UserDisplay.AvatarBg(User.Role)" Fg="@UserDisplay.AvatarFg(User.Role)" />
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The row this mark belongs to. Its token is the presence signal.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ExistingUser User { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether this principal holds <c>profile-images.read</c>. The token is the SUBJECT half of
    /// "renderable"; this is the CALLER half. Without it a 50-row render would fire fifty requests
    /// that all 403 — claims are baked into the auth cookie at sign-in, so a session that predates
    /// the claim's deploy does not hold it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool CanReadProfileImages { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// <c>""</c> in a list row, where the adjacent cell names the person; the subject's resolved
    /// display name in the detail panel, where the neighbour is a mono user id.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string Alt { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter] public OdsSize Size { get; set; } = OdsSize.Md;

    private bool _imageFailed;
    private Guid? _failedFor;

    private Guid? RenderableVersion => CanReadProfileImages ? User.ProfileImageVersion : null;

    private string? ImageSrc =>
        RenderableVersion is { } version ? ProfileApi.ImageUrl(User.Id, version) : null;

    private bool ShowImage =>
        ImageSrc is not null && !(_imageFailed && _failedFor == User.ProfileImageVersion);

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        // Keyed on the token rather than cleared unconditionally: re-rendering for an unrelated reason
        // (a sort, a filter) must not retry an image that is genuinely gone, but a replace must.
        if (_failedFor != User.ProfileImageVersion)
        {
            _imageFailed = false;
            _failedFor = null;
        }
    }

    private void OnImageError()
    {
        _imageFailed = true;
        _failedFor = User.ProfileImageVersion;
    }
}
